// ??0W3DModelDraw@@QAE@PAVThing@@PBVModuleData@@@Z
// partial score=0.6397 date=2026-09-29
// cl: /DNDEBUG /MD /EHsc /O2 /D_STLP_USE_STATIC_LIB /DBFME_STLP_NODE_ALLOC
// stlport
// BFME W3DModelDraw constructor, retail 0x00773360 (1185B).
//
// Identity: the body installs the W3DModelDraw vtables 0x01123D38 / 0x01123C68
// (and the pure-virtual ODI table 0x01123848) that the matched
// ??1W3DModelDraw@@MAE@XZ at 0x0077B090 installs, and calls
// ??0DrawableModule@@QAE@PAVThing@@PBVModuleData@@@Z (0x00113DA0) as its base,
// so this is W3DModelDraw::W3DModelDraw, not W3DScriptedModelDraw's.
//
// STATUS 2026-09-28: 0.978 instruction-shape agreement, 415 non-reloc byte
// diffs, first divergence at +0xf9.  Three verified fixes since the 0.45 bank,
// all measured with tools/probe.py:
//
//  1. The LOD selector is an UNSIGNED switch.  Retail ends it with
//     `cmp eax,4; ja` and a `jmp dword ptr [eax*4+table]`; the signed spelling
//     compiles to a compare chain AND costs the whole prologue: retail pushes
//     only ebx+esi and saves ebp/edi late, while the signed build pushes
//     ebx+ebp+esi+edi up front.  Casting the selector to unsigned removes the
//     extra early saves (876 -> 414 diffs, shape 0.867 -> 0.961).  This is the
//     single biggest lever found and it is not in docs/shape_levers.md.
//
//  2. The particle list at +0x48 holds a 20-BYTE element, not an int.  Retail
//     allocates a 0x1C node (`push 0x1c`) and the matched 0x0077B090
//     destructor frees the same node with `push 0x1c` +
//     ?_M_deallocate@?$__node_alloc@$00$0A@@_STL@@CAXPAXI@Z.  The matched
//     W3DModelDraw_updateSubObjectsFromShroud (0x00762500) only reads the ID at
//     node+8, so the remaining 16 bytes are unwitnessed; the element type keeps
//     the address token Rva00773360ParticleEntry rather than a guessed name.
//
//  3. The LOD switch assigns through a local that a `goto done` tail converges
//     on (variant u3).  This keeps one shared store and reaches shape 0.978
//     with 6 structural differences.  A separate `default:` label, five
//     distinct case bodies, an if/else chain and a plain local+single-store all
//     score worse (0.867-0.871): adding bodies makes VC7.1 emit a jump table,
//     but then it drops the epilogue shape retail has.
//
// REMAINING (6 structural differences, in address order):
//   a) +0xf9 `push edi` -- retail saves edi AFTER two of the six zero stores
//      at +0x130..+0x144; we save it before all six.  Every later offset is
//      therefore 2 bytes early, and the whole 0x2c0-0x49e tail shifts.  This
//      is the remaining blocker (regalloc).  Now DISPROVED as a source lever,
//      not merely untried: all five splits of the six stores between the two
//      opaque dword triples (1+5, 2+4, 3+3, 4+2, 5+1) emit BYTE-IDENTICAL
//      code (1179 B, 415 diffs, shape 0.978, 6 structural).  VC7.1 coalesces
//      the six adjacent `mov [esi+N],ebx` stores and hoists `push edi` above
//      the whole run regardless of how the source partitions them, so no
//      member/class/init-list spelling can place it after exactly two.
//      A second session re-disproved this from three other directions: the
//      2+4 and 2+2+2 MEMBER LAYOUTS implied by retail's own store split
//      (e), moving the four +0x138 stores into the ctor BODY (f), and
//      changing the number of live frame objects (i).  All keep +0xf9.
//   b) +0x2d6 retail keeps `jmp; xor ecx,ecx` for the null-drawable arm of the
//      indicator-colour test; we fold both null tests into one `je`.  Also
//      DISPROVED as a source lever: six further spellings (if/else statement
//      form, ternary inline at the use site, a `static Object * const` null,
//      a `volatile void *` member, a double-read `goto` form, and an
//      out-of-line `objectOrNull()` helper) all fold to the identical 415-diff
//      output.  VC7.1 propagates the drawable null through the phi, so the
//      two tests always merge; only a real ABI/EH change to the callee would
//      separate them.
//   c) +0x3d0 the `mov eax,0x3f800000` preload sits 0x16 bytes early.  Four
//      more spellings measured no effect: an extra trailing statement, an
//      extra nested block, a `const float one` local, and a
//      `static const float kIdentity[12]` table.  The table form DOES cut raw
//      diffs 415->366 but only by shrinking the body to 1129 B (loop instead
//      of retail's twelve straight stores), so it is a regression, not a lever.
//   d) +0x43d the dispatch tail.  CORRECTION to the earlier note in this
//      file: the banked source DOES emit retail's `cmp eax,4 / ja / jmp
//      [eax*4+0x773804]` jump table WITH the three duplicated epilogues, so
//      the two goals are NOT mutually exclusive -- an earlier session read
//      the residue as "compare chain, no table" from a different variant.
//      The real residue is one extra instruction pair: ours peels
//      `cmp eax,1 / pop edi / jbe 0x460` and puts a FOURTH copy of the
//      "mov eax,2; mov [esi+0xa0],eax" epilogue at +0x460, where retail
//      falls straight through its `cmp eax,4` test.  Retail's table
//      0x00773804 was read directly: entries 0,1 -> +0x446; 2 -> +0x466;
//      3,4 -> +0x486, so 3 distinct targets over 5 labels, and retail has
//      no lower-bound peel.  Nine further switch spellings (h) never remove
//      the peel, and the four slot-pointer/reference forms that would give
//      the store a register source instead of an immediate (g) all fold back
//      to the immediate.  This is a VC7.1 switch-lowering decision.
//
// tools/eh_levers.py (throw() per callee, /EHsc, _STLP_NO_EXCEPTIONS) and
// tools/shape_family_levers.py over all ten families were both run against
// this source and shape_search.py plateaued at 7 and 9 trials with no
// improving output.  One session added 29 further measured variants across
// the store-split, null-conditional, constant-preload, LOD-switch and
// body-store families (see (a)-(d) above); every one landed on either the
// identical 415-diff output or a documented regression.  The residue is
// compiler-internal register allocation, not a missing source lever.
//
// SESSION 3 (2026-09-29) added 21 more measured variants, all with
// tools/probe.py --shape, none improving on 1179 B / 415 diffs / shape 0.978:
//
//  e) DISPROVED the "member boundary creates the push edi split" reading of
//     (a).  Retail's six zero stores are 2+4, not 3+3, which suggested an
//     8-byte member at +0x130 and a 16-byte member at +0x138.  Measured: a
//     2-dword + 4-dword member pair (v1), three separate 2-dword class
//     objects at +0x130/+0x138/+0x140 (y1), and a POD byte-array middle
//     (y2).  All three keep push edi at +0xf9.  So the split is NOT a member
//     boundary either; the previous session's 1+5..5+1 store partitions and
//     this session's class-shape variants agree, and the split is an
//     artefact of the scheduler, not of the layout.
//  f) DISPROVED the init-list/body boundary as the (a) lever.  Moving the
//     four stores at +0x138 out of the initializer list into body statements,
//     with and without a nested block (p1b, p2b), drops the body to 1161 B
//     with 774 diffs and deletes the whole +0x130..+0x16c run from the shape
//     list: the body stores are hoisted above the base-class initialisation.
//  g) DISPROVED the slot-pointer/reference spellings of the LOD store.  Four
//     forms (int *slot in the block, the same with plain break, int &slot,
//     and a function-scope slot pointer) all emit the IDENTICAL 413-diff
//     output: VC7.1 rewrites `*slot = 2` back to an immediate store, so
//     retail's `mov eax,2; mov [esi+0xa0],eax` is not reachable this way.
//  h) RE-MEASURED the LOD switch as a joint goal.  A plain switch with a
//     direct member store per case body (w1) does reach 413 diffs and DOES
//     get the jump table, but it costs 3 extra structural differences and
//     drops shape to 0.961, and the peel is still there.  The measured
//     frontier is therefore 413 diffs at shape 0.961 (w1/g/x1-x4/s2) versus
//     415 diffs at shape 0.978 (the banked form); the byte gate accepts
//     neither, and the bank keeps the higher-shape form.  Nine further
//     switch spellings (default-first, no default label, all-goto, all-break,
//     pre-initialised local, reversed case order, an if/else ladder, an
//     enum-typed selector, a direct-store goto tail: z1-z4, q1-q4, s2, s3)
//     score 863-873 diffs and 13-22 structural differences, all worse.
//  i) DISPROVED frame-object count as an allocator lever.  docs/shape_levers.md
//     ("retail had one more object") predicts that changing the number of
//     live objects moves the save placement.  Measured: an extra volatile
//     Object* local live across the colour and matrix phases (r1), an extra
//     volatile matrix pointer (r2), and an extra 16-byte aggregate frame
//     object (r3).  All three emit the byte-identical 415-diff output, so the
//     push edi position is not sensitive to the number of frame objects.
//  j) DISPROVED local-elimination as a lever.  Replacing the module/draw
//     temporaries with direct re-reads of the members (s1, the
//     "read the member again" lever) and putting the LOD selector in its own
//     nested block (s3) both leave the output unchanged.
//
// Net: 50 measured variants across three sessions, none improving.  The
// residue at (a)-(d) is VC7.1 register allocation and switch lowering, not a
// missing source spelling.  Reopen only with a NEW witness for the +0x130
// member layout, a different EH frame shape, or a toolchain observation that
// contradicts (d).
//
// The public ZH header stops at the first few pointers; the member ordering
// below follows the retail constructor/destructor packet and the 17-state EH
// map at 0x00773360 (tools/eh_info.py): particle list +0x48, set +0x8c, four
// 12-byte recoil vectors +0xac, three 0x1c slots +0xdc, opaque triples
// +0x130/+0x13c, ten-dword zero packet +0x148, decal pairs
// +0x178/+0x1bc, two layout strings at +0x200/+0x204 and the 1.0f matrix tail
// at +0x234..+0x268.

